Review fixes (6 November 2026): report and analysis only, no new runs, no service code changed.

1. CPU split per service
   analyze_official.py adds cpu_order, cpu_inventory, cpu_worker, cpu_services and cpu_infra.
   Each is the process_cpu_seconds_total increase over the load window, as a share of the
   2-vCPU host. Infrastructure is the host CPU minus the three services. These feed the new
   table tab-cpu.tex (Results, Resource Use, tab:results-cpu).
2. Publisher wording
   The Results and Discussion no longer say "per-message confirm". The publisher claims 50 rows,
   pipelines their confirms on one channel and loops at once while batches are full. The stated
   limit is now one serial loop per service, running in the API's process.
3. Rates
   New done_load_per_s: orders reaching Completed or Rejected per second during the load
   (C1: requests decided). The throughput table adds it and the 99 % done time. Completed/s is
   footnoted as including the reconciliation wait.
4. Worker dead letters
   These are now presented as a defect the experiment found. The fix (back-pressure, a longer
   ladder or a shorter Confirmed timeout) is stated as not implemented because of the freeze.
5. Discussion
   New section sec:dis-c1-wins: why C1 wins on this host, and when the asynchronous design would.
6. Limitations
   Four additions: contention not varied; shedding limits not calibrated; REJECTED not recorded
   in Redis; processed:{product} unbounded.
7. Restructure
   - Introduction, Problem Statement and Objectives are now one chapter; Scope and Limitations
     are now one chapter.
   - Week and step labels are removed from headings.
   - Moved to appendices: the pilot, the slowdown diagnosis and the EC2 confirmation
     (Appendix C); the pilot results (C); the external review (D); the verification summary,
     the workflow evidence, the Worker/observability verification and the preliminary overload
     run (B).
   - The re-freeze detail moved into the Freeze Manifest appendix.
   - The failure-model table no longer overflows (it was 13 pt wide).
   - Main text is pages 7-105 (99 pages); the PDF has 133 pages. See build.log.

